ARCHITECTURE NOTES (faithful port, native-idiomatic)
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  • Source-seam + @Observable model (DBHealthPageModel) consuming a DBHealthSource (P1/S8);
    NO networking/business logic in the view. Three web reads (useDBStats /dev-tools/db-stats,
    useMigrations /dev-tools/migration-status, useConnectionPool /dev-tools/runtime-info)
    coalesced into one DBHealthUpdate, each with its own load status → per-source phase.
  • Hook names preserved at the Swift seam intent: statsStatus/stats, migrationStatus/migration,
    poolStatus/pool on DBHealthUpdate map 1:1 to useDBStats/useMigrations/useConnectionPool.
  • Pure, dependency-free Adapter + Projection (Foundation only): web formatBytes ramp, the
    100 MB large-table threshold, the size|rows|name sort with the `sizeBytes ?? rowCount`
    fallback, the top-15 chart memo with 18-char+ellipsis truncation, pool usage %, and the
    reverse-chronological recent migrations — all unit-tested.
  • Adaptive (ADR-006): NavigationStack scaffold; tables panel beside the migration+pool
    sidebar on regular widths (macOS/iPad), stacked on compact iPhone; table renders as a native
    Grid on regular widths and stacked cards on compact.
  • Design tokens only (P2 Color.TS / Font.TS / TSSpacing / TSRadius) — no hardcoded colors;
    GlassPanel via the shared TSGlassPanel material (ADR-005).
  • i18n (ADR-014): every visible literal via LocalizedStringKey / the DBHealthStrings facade;
    zero hardcoded English; web key names kept verbatim; 43 keys added to Localizable.xcstrings
    (41 parity + 2 freshness) and 6 shared-component support keys the surface surfaces
    (action.retry, chart.copyData/export/noData, error.queryTitle/queryMessage).
  • a11y (ADR-015): accessibilityLabel/value/traits on panels, chart bars, sort toggle, rows;
    Dynamic Type via the Font.TS ramp; Reduce-Motion honored in the chart + FadeIn; light/dark +
    increased-contrast via the dynamic token colors.
  • Native additions over the web, all prompt-mandated and stated (no silent drift): the ADR-013
    freshness chip (stale/offline) + one-shot guarded stale auto-refresh, and an inline pool
    error+retry (the web pool read has no error branch).
  • Navigation: /db-health is a standalone web route, not a curated top-level AppRoute (whose set
    is exhaustively asserted by MenuCommandCatalogTests == AppRoute.allCases). Registered
    additively as a SwiftUI NavigationDestination value (DBHealthRoute, path "/db-health",
    .dbHealthNavigationDestination(makeModel:)) — reachable from any NavigationStack, the curated
    route set + its tests untouched. Parsed/round-tripped in DBHealthRouteTests.

